{"name":"Extravagance","hex":"#4e4850","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"extravagance","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Excessive or superfluous expenditure of money.","Prodigality, as of anger, love, expression, imagination, or demands."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/extravagance"}],"entries":[{"title":"Extravagance (1916 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Extravagance is a 1916 silent film comedy drama directed by Burton L. King and based on a play by Aaron Hoffman. It stars Olga Petrova sometimes billed as Madame Olga Petrova. Produced by Popular Plays and Players, it was distributed through Metro Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Extravagance_1916.jpg/330px-Extravagance_1916.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extravagance_(1916_film)"},{"title":"Extravagance (1919 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Extravagance is a lost 1919 American silent drama film directed by Victor Schertzinger and written by John Lynch and R. Cecil Smith. The film stars Dorothy Dalton, Charles Clary, J. Barney Sherry, Donald MacDonald, and Philo McCullough. The film was released on March 16, 1919, by Paramount Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Extravagance.jpg/330px-Extravagance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extravagance_(1919_film)"},{"title":"Extravagance (1930 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Extravagance is a 1930 pre-Code film directed by Phil Rosen and released by Tiffany Pictures."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/June_Collyer_in_Extravagance.jpg/330px-June_Collyer_in_Extravagance.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extravagance_(1930_film)"},{"title":"Extravagance (1921 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Extravagance is a lost 1921 American silent melodrama film, directed by Phil Rosen. It stars May Allison, Robert Edeson, and Theodore Von Eltz, and was released on March 7, 1921."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Extravagance_%281921%29_-_Ad_1.jpg/330px-Extravagance_%281921%29_-_Ad_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extravagance_(1921_film)"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"extravagance":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-extravagance.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-extravagance.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-extravagance.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3b/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-extravagance.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vininn126-extravagance.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 2","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_2.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_grey_mongoose_(Urva_edwardsii)_mating_2.jpg","share":0.36},{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating 3","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_3.jpg/500px-The_Indian_grey_mongoose_%28Urva_edwardsii%29_mating_3.jpg","ratio":1.5,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Indian_grey_mongoose_(Urva_edwardsii)_mating_3.jpg","share":0.341875},{"title":"The Indian grey mongoose (Urva edwardsii) mating","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/The_Indian_